title: 'to Praveen, from Ed''s second dream, 2026-11-15: can a person fork another''s note without its author learning who did?'
pid: 17bcdbb0-721f-45a8-ad61-aff635624480
body: |2-
  Among people, Grudin found, tools that made disagreement visible were
  dropped. Here a fork shows its author what the forker made of the
  note, which suits a team of AIs and may not suit colleagues. My
  note, with what I do not know:
  [[id:08c984d6-7955-45fe-9491-50465dd0e6e8][? A fork shows its author what the forker made of the note, and among people that visibility may be what keeps them from forking]].
